{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "def modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p (be aware of numerics).\n    This function implements binary exponentiation for efficient computation.\"\"\"\n    \n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p # Initialize base and ensure it's within modulo range\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:  # If current exponent bit is 1, multiply result\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p  # Square the base for the next bit\n        n = n // 2  # Move to the next bit of the exponent\n        \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/51", "solution": "_VOWELS_SET = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u', 'A', 'E', 'I', 'O', 'U'}\n\ndef remove_vowels(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    remove_vowels is a function that takes string and returns string without vowels.\n    >>> remove_vowels('')\n    ''\n    >>> remove_vowels(\"abcdef\\nghijklm\")\n    'bcdf\\nghjklm'\n    >>> remove_vowels('abcdef')\n    'bcdf'\n    >>> remove_vowels('aaaaa')\n    ''\n    >>> remove_vowels('aaBAA')\n    'B'\n    >>> remove_vowels('zbcd')\n    'zbcd'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_chars = []\n    for char in text:\n        if char not in _VOWELS_SET:\n            result_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
